"""CAR INTELLIGENCE — identify the car + split a flat livery into self-built LAYERS (2026-06-26).

Goal (owner): load a flat TGA, figure out WHICH iRacing car it is, then auto-build layers:
  NUMBERS  - the car number(s)            (OCR, smart_separate)
  SPONSORS - logos / wordmarks            (OCR, smart_separate)
  TEMPLATE - the car's fixed bits         (lights / grills / windows / reserved low-variance regions,
                                           learned per car-model from the livery stack variance)
  PAINT    - the creative paint design     (everything else)

Car identity + the per-car TEMPLATE prior come from _car_intel/<car_slug>/ (built by _car_intel_learn.py:
signature.npz {med 64x64 luma, std 64x64, template_frac} + template_mask.png). Fully ADDITIVE + lazy;
degrades gracefully when the intel library or OCR is absent. Returns uint8 masks (255=member) at input res.
"""
